WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.610
Energy drains are the conditions that make useful work more expensive than it needs to be.

2
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.799
Unclear priorities force repeated decisions about what matters.

3
00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:16.083
Open loops keep unresolved tasks, questions, commitments, or decisions active in the background.

4
00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:18.402
Multitasking fragments attention.

5
00:00:18.402 --> 00:00:20.945
Constant availability prevents depth.

6
00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:26.930
Excessive meetings consume not only time, but also preparation, social energy, and recovery.

7
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.398
Unresolved conflict is another drain.

8
00:00:29.398 --> 00:00:37.253
Even when people avoid talking about it, conflict can absorb emotional energy, distort communication, and slow decisions.

9
00:00:37.253 --> 00:00:44.060
Cluttered environments can create friction when tools, files, information, or next steps are hard to find.

10
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.324
Poor boundaries turn every request into a potential interruption.

11
00:00:48.324 --> 00:00:54.757
Rework drains energy because people have to pay again for work that could have been clarified earlier.

12
00:00:54.757 --> 00:00:58.048
Hidden emotional labor is often invisible in plans.

13
00:00:58.048 --> 00:01:09.194
It includes smoothing tension, remembering interpersonal context, supporting others through uncertainty, absorbing complaints, or managing the emotional tone of a group.

14
00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:12.860
This work can be valuable, but it still consumes capacity.

15
00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:20.116
When it is not acknowledged, people may feel depleted without being able to point to a visible task that explains it.

16
00:01:20.116 --> 00:01:22.434
Small drains compound across a week.

17
00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:31.112
A few extra status meetings, a cluttered task list, unclear ownership, and constant message checking may not look dramatic in isolation.

18
00:01:31.112 --> 00:01:35.600
Together, they can consume the capacity needed for high-quality work.

19
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.490
Before assuming a motivation problem, look for energy leaks.

20
00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:46.896
The practical question is what can be clarified, closed, batched, delegated, automated, simplified, or protected.
